### Requesting Adjustments

At DLA Piper, we aim to make meaningful progress and build an inclusive culture where anyone affected by disability, neurodiversity or a long-term health condition has an equitable and accessible chance of success. If you think you may need adjustments or additional support to enable you to participate in our recruitment process, please contact our **Recruitment team** and we will be happy to support you.

### Agile Working

We recognise that people have responsibilities and interests outside of their career and that as a business, we all benefit from working flexibly. That’s why we are open to discussing with candidates the different ways in which we are able to support requests for agile working arrangements.

### Pre-Engagement Screening

In the event that we make an offer to you, and where local legislation permits, we will conduct pre-engagement screening checks that may include but are not limited to your professional and academic qualifications, your eligibility to work in the relevant jurisdiction, any criminal records, your financial stability, and references from previous employers.

## Our hiring approach

Our hiring approach enables us to learn about the professional and person you are, and gives you the opportunity to learn about us. Your recruitment experience can differ depending on the type of role you are interviewing for. You will always meet your direct Line Manager for your role, as well as peers and close collaborators for the position. For some of our roles we may also use assessment tools, practical exercises, and panel presentations. Your Recruitment Business Partner will inform you of the recruitment process at the start of any recruitment process, but please let us know if you have any questions prior to making an application.

# Marketing Intern

## Job Details

**Salary:** £27,000

**Work Pattern:** Full Time, Hybrid Working, with approval

**Location:** Kemble, Gloucester, GL7 6BQ

---

## **About FleetCheck**

At FleetCheck we believe that everyone has the right to be safe on the roads and we are all about making a difference to road safety. Our business was created to improve the safety of drivers and vehicles by providing the tools and support that promote professional fleet management.

Our business is all about serving others, focused on the common good and we get there through consideration and respect for each other. Our customers trust us to deliver excellence. They trust us because they experience outstanding software provided by people who are dependable and prepared to go that extra mile.

This is a growing business, and we need people who are open to new opportunities and experiences, ready to learn new things and help drive the business forward. The enthusiasm, honesty, and openness here is infectious and it helps us hit problems head on and be determined to find the best solutions.

## **General Overview**

This is a 12-month internship for someone who wants hands on experience in B2B marketing. You won’t be assigned to one area, over the year you’ll work across events, content, social media, research and design, picking up whatever needs doing that week. It suits an all-rounder: someone keen, organised and happy to roll their sleeves up, whether that’s designing a social graphic in the morning or packing boxes for a trade show in the afternoon. You’ll get plenty of support, and as you find your feet you’ll be trusted to run pieces of work yourself.

**What you’ll do (but not limited to)**

**Events**

* Help plan and deliver our trade shows, webinars and our annual customer conference;
* Look after the logistics: stand kit, printed materials, venue details, delegate lists, hotel bookings;
* Be there on the day, talking to fleet managers and helping things run smoothly;
* Develop and deliver engaging post event communications.

**Content and campaigns**

* Write and edit blog posts, guides, case studies and email newsletters;
* Read industry news items to find stories worth telling;
* Help keep our website and content hub up to date;
* Help coordinate our marketing campaigns, keeping track of what’s going out and when, then report on how each one performed.

**Social media**

* Plan, write and schedule posts, mainly on LinkedIn;
* Create short videos and graphics for social;
* Keep an eye on comments and engagement, and report on how posts perform.

**Research**

* Keep up with what’s happening in the fleet and transport world, from DVSA and O-licence changes to EV adoption;
* Look into competitors and what they’re saying;
* Help gather customer feedback and pull together findings we can use in campaigns.

**Design**

* Create simple social graphics, email headers and presentation slides, working from our brand templates;
* Brief and work with our designers on bigger pieces such as brochures and event materials;
* Check that everything we put out looks and sounds like FleetCheck. If design is your thing, there’s plenty of room to take on more.

## What we need

* A degree in Marketing, Communications, or a related subject, or equivalent qualification or experience;
* Excellent written communication skills, with strong spelling, grammar and attention to detail;
* Confidence communicating with a range of people, both over the phone and face to face;
* Strong organisational skills, with the ability to manage multiple priorities and meet deadlines;
* A proactive and self-motivated approach, with a willingness to learn and ask questions;
* Initiative and a problem-solving mindset, with the confidence to take ownership of tasks;
* Resilience and tenacity when faced with challenges;
* Curiosity about business and a genuine interest in marketing.

**It would also be great if you also had:**

* Experience creating content or managing social media accounts for a club, society, business or personal project;
* An interest in graphic design and experience using Adobe Creative Suite;
* A portfolio showcasing design, content creation or marketing work from your studies, employment or personal projects.

## What you’ll get out of it

* A year of hands-on experience across a wide range of marketing activities;
* The opportunity to contribute to real campaigns, events, content and design projects from day one;
* A portfolio of live work that you can showcase throughout your future career;
* Regular one-to-one coaching with the Head of Marketing, alongside support from the wider marketing team;
* Exposure to different areas of marketing to help you discover where your strengths and interests lie;
* The chance to develop practical skills and commercial experience in a fast-growing SaaS business.

## How to apply

Please send the following to recruitment@fleetcheck.co.uk :

* Your CV
* A short note on why this role appeals to you and what you think you can bring to it
* Links to any social media accounts you run or have been part of, such as for a club, society, business, or yourself
* If you have them, some examples of your work

**Rewards and additional information**

* Base salary will be in the region of £27k pa,
* The normal contractual working week is 37.5 hours; a standard day is 7.5 hours. The work pattern is fixed hours of 9.00am to 5.00pm with 0.5 hour lunch break.
* The annual holiday entitlement based on the above working pattern is 25 days.
* 1 additional days holiday per month on a Friday (FleetCheck Friday), pro rata entitlement for part time employees.
* Contributory pension.
* Staff can work in a hybrid pattern, Monday to Wednesday being office based; with the option to work from home on Thursdays and Fridays if agreed with their line manager.
* Other benefits include – staff/team functions, including Summer & Winter events, monthly charity cake bakes, monthly staff meetings, regular performance reviews, access to
* Employee Assistance
* Program (EAP), Mental Health First Aiders, free parking.
* The organisation continuously evolves to provide broader and more proactive customer care. As such the roles and their terms and conditions will be subject to ongoing review and change.
* FleetCheck are proud to be a Disability Confident Employer and a Living Wage Employer.

**Successful candidates will be required to undertake a BPSS check.**

*Note that the FleetCheck offices are not serviced by public transport. You will need a full clean driving licence and a car to work here.*

**Employee Promise**

FleetCheck is all about helping others, focused on a common good and we get there through consideration and respect for each other. Our clients trust us to deliver excellence. They trust us because they experience outstanding software and people who are dependable and prepared to go that extra mile when it is needed.

We are a growing business, and we need people who are open to new opportunities and experiences, ready to learn new things and help drive the business forward. The enthusiasm, honesty, and openness here is infectious and it helps us solve problems head on and be determined to find solutions, helping our customers, and improving our products.

Excellent client experience is our goal, and we need people who will do what they say, deliver on their promises and look for ways to surprise or even delight with the unexpected. If you yearn for a sense of togetherness, mutual respect, and loyalty, and will work hard as part of a community to foster a deep collaborative approach, we are the place for you.

**Privacy Notice**

This privacy notice tells you what to expect when FleetCheck collects your personal information.

When individuals apply to work at FleetCheck, we will only use the information they supply to us to process their application and to monitor recruitment statistics. Where we want to disclose information to a third party, for example where we want to take up a reference, we will not do so without informing them beforehand unless the disclosure is required by law.

Personal information about unsuccessful candidates will be held for 12 months after the recruitment exercise has been completed, it will then be destroyed or deleted. We may retain de-personalised statistical information about applicants to help inform our recruitment activities, but no individuals would be identifiable from that data.

FleetCheck collects and processes a range of information supplied by you. This may include:

* + - * + - * + - Your name, address and contact details, including email address and telephone number;
                - Details of your qualifications, skills, experience and employment history, including start and end dates, with previous employers;
                - Information about your nationality and entitlement to work in the UK;

We may also collect, store and use sensitive personal information supplied by you, including:

* + - * + - * + - Information about medical or health conditions, including whether you have a disability for which the organisation needs to make reasonable adjustments.

**AI**

While we encourage people to use AI systems during their role to help them work faster and more effectively, please do not use AI assistants during the application process.

We want the information you present to FleetCheck to support your employment application to be your own thoughts, facts and opinions without mediation through an AI system, and we also want to evaluate your non-AI-assisted communication skills.

## How to apply

If you would like to bring your skills, energy and dedication to be part of our friendly and enthusiastic team or would like to apply for any open positions, email recruitment@fleetcheck.co.uk with a covering letter and CV.

# IT Technical Recruiter (contractor)

London, United Kingdom

Grid Dynamics is looking for a (contractor) Technical Recruiter in our London office. We would like to strengthen our recruitment team with a proactive and result-oriented person, who easily connects with people and has a passion for finding the best talents. The hiring focus will be on technical roles of Middle and Senior level. You will be a part of an international recruitment team sharing common goals and values.

Essential functions

* Manage full cycle of recruitment process for technical positions;
* Active search of candidates using different sources and recruitment strategies;
* Provide regular updates to recruitment lead and hiring manager about the recruitment pipelines, market capacity, availability of candidates, salary ranges, etc;
* Create job descriptions, manage job posts and requisitions in our ATS;
* Work with hiring managers and interviewers to streamline the hiring process;
* Close cooperation with staffing team to identify hiring priorities and adjust recruitment efforts based on them;
* Keep data accuracy and timely update recruitment tool;
* Highlight issues/bottlenecks in the recruitment process, create an improvement action plan and put it into action.

Qualifications

* At least 5 years of experience as technical recruiter on local IT market;
* Proven track record of hiring technical positions;
* Growing network and visible activity on Linkedin profile;
* Knowledge of local market specifics, competitors, salaries and market trends;
* High level of self-motivation and proactivity;
* Flexibility and multitasking;
* Strong communication, presentation, negotiation skills;
* Willingness to dedicate time for self-education;
* Ability to work with ATS, recruitments tools and basic analytics;

Would be a plus

* Experience in banking and fintech.
* Experience working in a software consultancy or similar services business.
* Experience from the agency side.

We offer

* Opportunity to work on bleeding-edge projects
* Work with a highly motivated and dedicated team
* Competitive salary
* Flexible schedule
* Benefits package - medical insurance, sports
* Corporate social events
* Professional development opportunities
* Well-equipped office

About us

Grid Dynamics (NASDAQ: GDYN) is a leading provider of technology consulting, platform and product engineering, AI, and advanced analytics services. Fusing technical vision with business acumen, we solve the most pressing technical challenges and enable positive business outcomes for enterprise companies undergoing business transformation. A key differentiator for Grid Dynamics is our 8 years of experience and leadership in enterprise AI, supported by profound expertise and ongoing investment in data, analytics, cloud & DevOps, application modernization and customer experience. Founded in 2006, Grid Dynamics is headquartered in Silicon Valley with offices across the Americas, Europe, and India.

Mizuho | Greenhill - Private Capital Advisory Associate

#

## Mizuho | Greenhill - Private Capital Advisory Associate

Apply

:   UK - London

:   Full time

:   Posted Yesterday

:   R7167

Greenhill & Co. is a leading independent investment bank focused on providing financial advice on significant mergers, acquisitions, restructurings, financings, liquidity solutions and capital raisings to corporations, partnerships, institutions and governments. Greenhill operates globally from offices in New York, London, Frankfurt, Madrid, Stockholm, Sydney, Toronto, Chicago, Hong Kong, Houston, Los Angeles, Melbourne, Paris, San Francisco, Singapore.

In November 2023, Greenhill was acquired by Mizuho Financial Group.

Mizuho | Greenhill's Private Capital Advisory team (“PCA”) advises institutional investors and fund sponsors across the private markets’ ecosystem on primary fundraising and secondary liquidity solutions. Within the PCA business, the Secondary Advisory team specialises in asset-, fund-, and sponsor-level transactions, delivering tailored secondary solutions to support portfolio management, fund structuring and liquidity objectives. Since 2001, our secondary team has advised on more than $420 billion of private equity secondary transactions – more than any other advisor. Combining deep market insight, extensive transaction experience and a research-driven, analytical approach, the team partners with many of the world’s most sophisticated institutional investors and fund sponsors to achieve their strategic, capital and liquidity objectives.

**Job Description**

The PCA team are seeing an Associate to join our team in London. The Associate will play a key role in the origination and execution of a broad range of LP-led and GP-led transactions, including portfolio sales, continuation vehicles, preferred equity solutions, GP stakes transactions and other structured liquidity solutions. Working closely with both senior bankers and junior team members, the Associate will support the execution of client mandates across all stages of the advisory process, helping to deliver strategic advice and successful transaction outcomes.

Key responsibilities include:

* Support all aspects of transaction execution across a broad range of secondary transactions:
  + Perform due diligence on underlying funds and portfolio companies, including analysis of financial performance, operating metrics, capital structures, valuation and industry dynamics;
  + Develop and review financial models and valuation analyses to support transaction execution and structuring;
  + Prepare and review client and marketing materials, including confidential information memoranda, valuation analyses, process documentation and due diligence responses;
  + Assist with investor outreach, coordinate investor due diligence processes, manage information flow, respond to investor requests and support transaction timelines;
  + Participate in client meetings, management presentations and investor discussions, presenting transaction analyses and key findings as required; and
  + Help drive transaction execution through signing and closing, coordinating workstreams across clients, investors and external advisers.
* Conduct market, transaction and industry research to support business development activities and broader understanding of private markets and secondary market dynamics;
* Support the preparation of new business presentations, pitch materials and client proposals;
* Produce and maintain various internal transaction databases and market intelligence resources;
* Review work product prepared by Analysts and Interns and contribute to their development through coaching, training and mentoring;
* Develop relationships with market participants across the secondary ecosystem, including investors, fund sponsors, advisers and legal counsel; and
* Coordinate with other colleagues across the wider PCA platform and Mizuho | Greenhill's industry coverage and product teams.



**Knowledge, Qualifications and Experience**

* Bachelor’s degree with a strong academic record from a leading university;
* 3–5 years of experience in investment banking, secondary advisory, private equity, private markets investing, asset management or strategy consulting;
* Demonstrated interest in both LP-led and GP-led transactions;
* Strong understanding of financial analysis, valuation methodologies and corporate finance principles;
* Advanced financial modelling and analytical capabilities;
* Excellent communication and presentation skills;
* Strong project management and organisational skills, with the ability to manage multiple workstreams simultaneously;
* A strong work ethic, intellectual curiosity and a collaborative, team-oriented approach;
* Leadership potential and commitment to mentoring junior team members;
* Fluency in an additional European language is advantageous.

**Greenhill: Diversity, Opportunity and Inclusion**

As part of working with Internationally minded clients, often as part of a close cross-border collaboration with other Mizuho | Greenhill offices, fostering diversity of thought throughout the firm is of significant importance to Greenhill.  This importance drives a recruitment strategy that seeks to identify candidates based on their capabilities and affinity to a collaboration-based team environment, as well as the cultural value-add they can bring to our firm.

*Job description subject to change upon Manager’s discretion*

#LI-Onsite

#GHL

Greenhill & Co., Inc., part of Mizuho Americas, is focused on providing financial advice on significant mergers, acquisitions, restructurings, financings and capital raising to corporations, partnerships, institutions and governments globally. It acts on behalf of clients throughout the world from its offices in the Americas, EMEA, and APAC.

Portman Finance Group | Graduate Scheme

# Portman Autumn Careers Fair Durham

Northampton, United Kingdom | Posted on 19/10/2026

