## Job Description

An incredible opportunity for a motivated, driven and commercially astute graduate to rapidly progress their career within a fast growing, meritocratic and dynamic finance firm.

As a Graduate Finance Broker, you will be contacting potential clients through outbound calls, positioning Portman Finance Group’s financial solutions in a consultative manner and passing qualified leads to our busy Sales Team. With an annual starting salary ranging from £36,000 to £50,000 (depending on academic background and interview performance), we are looking for someone who has a natural flair to build telephone rapport alongside the ability to drive sales processes to completion and achieve key KPI targets in a highly competitive and lucrative environment.

**Please do not apply if you consider yourself more of an analyst as this role will not be right for you.**

Responsibilities

* Conduct outbound sales activity to establish rapport and interest with potential new clients, ultimately building a pipeline and securing new business opportunities;
* With a customer-centric approach, qualify client interest through a consultative sales process to understand their commercial standing and position Portman’s financial solutions;
* Write and prepare proposal documentation and credit applications as and when required, including working with clients to gather appropriate financial and non-financial paperwork;
* Record all sales activity in our CRM;
* Build and maintain a pipeline of live opportunities; and
* Any other appropriate job duties in line with the associated skill and experience of the post holder.



### Requirements

Skills & Experience Required

* Motivated and driven individuals with a passion for sales;
* Ability to communicate clearly and concisely whilst building rapport and trust;
* Minimum of ABB at A Level and a 2.1 or above University Degree across any discipline;
* Resilient with the capability to work under pressure in a fast-paced meritocratic environment;
* Strong commercial acumen, with an interest in business;
* Dynamic individuals with an entrepreneurial, self-starter approach; and
* Positive and engaging telephone manner.

Personal Attributes

* Success and winning motivated. If coming third is good enough for you, please do not apply;
* Excellent written and oral communications skills;
* Ability to build strong and effective working relationships at all levels, including senior stakeholders;
* Adept at problem-solving with a can-do attitude;
* Strong organisational skills with a high attention to detail;
* Ability to prioritise and handle multiple tasks at any given time; and
* Ability to work on own initiative as well as being a team player.



### Benefits

* Very competitive salary and incentives;
* Rapid career progression;
* Vibrant office culture with break out lounge, bar and corporate days out;
* 1-1 training and mentoring;
* Meritocratic culture; and
* Performance recognition.

# Career Opportunities: Senior Agentic AI Engineer (11465)

Requisition ID **11465** - Posted **10/26/2026** - Years of Experience (3) - **Technology** - Where (1) - **Job**

  Job Description Print Preview



Senior Agentic AI Engineer

Data Reply, a young and dynamic company within the Reply group specialising in Big Data, Artificial Intelligence, Data Governance and Quantum Computing, is looking for a Senior Agentic AI Engineer.

Responsibilities

* Design, implement and optimise Agentic AI and GenAI solutions for our clients, from architecture definition through to production release;
* Work closely with clients to understand their business goals, translating complex data challenges into clear requirements and concrete, high-impact solutions

* Lead the different project phases, ensuring the quality and scalability of the models developed and deployed to production.
* Define and run evaluation strategies for LLM-based systems to guarantee reliable and measurable behaviour over time;
* Integrate agents with client systems and third-party services, working with DevOps teams and the client to identify and resolve architectural inconsistencies;
* Act as a technical guide for the team, setting engineering standards and ensuring code quality through structured review processes.

Requirements

Education and experience:

* Bachelor's or Master's degree in Computer Science, Computer Engineering or a related field;

* At least 4–5 years of experience in software development or ML/AI, including at least 1–2 years on LLM-based projects and agentic solutions deployed to production;

* Experience in consulting or client-facing environments.

Tech skills:

* Excellent command of Python and of the main frameworks for building agentic systems (e.g. LangGraph, Semantic Kernel, AutoGen) including multi-agent design: orchestration, routing between specialised agents and conversational state management;
* Excellent command of Python and of the main frameworks for agentic systems (e.g. LangGraph, Semantic Kernel, AutoGen), including multi-agent design: orchestration, routing between specialised agents and conversational state management;
* Solid experience in prompt engineering and LLM evaluation (ground truth, relevance metrics, regression testing);
* In-depth knowledge of RAG architectures (hybrid and vector-based) and the ability to assess their trade-offs;
* Implementation of guardrails and security measures for LLM systems, including protection against prompt injection;
* API design (REST, SSE streaming, interface contracts, versioning) and integration of agents with external systems via tools and function calling, covering authentication, error handling, data validation and abstraction layers; knowledge of MCP is a plus;
* Knowledge of the main Cloud services for AI solutions (including security, identity and monitoring) and the ability to build systems with scalability, resilience, observability and cost in mind;

Soft skills:

* Ability to listen to clients and analyse their needs, understanding their business goals and turning them into clear, actionable requirements;

* Ability to act as the client's technical point of reference with a critical eye: managing expectations, dependencies and blockers, and communicating risks and trade-offs;

* Autonomy and ownership: ability to make technical decisions and stand behind them;

* Full professional proficiency in English for daily client interactions and technical documentation.

What does it mean to be a Dater?

Continuous learning 💡   
You'll have the opportunity to attend a range of courses and certifications to enrich your professional and technical background.

Life in Data 🏄   
Data Reply gives its Daters the chance to take part in company events and become part of the team. The company cares about people's wellbeing and promotes a healthy work-life balance.

Go beyond your limits 🚀   
You'll challenge yourself every day in fast-evolving, dynamic fields, pushing yourself beyond your limits.

What we offer

* An offer built around your career path. The salary offer will be defined based on the position, your professional experience, your technical skills, the level of responsibility the role involves and the organisational context you'll join. At Reply we mainly apply the Italian National Collective Labour Agreement for the Metalworking Industry (CCNL Metalmeccanica Industria). Entry is from level B2, with a gross annual salary (RAL) between €37,000 and €65,000.

* A structured growth path. Our Career Path offers growth opportunities in both technical and managerial roles. Your aspirations, the skills you develop and the results you achieve will shape your path.

*Reply is committed to embracing diversity and creating an inclusive work environment by valuing the uniqueness of people regardless of age, gender, sexual orientation, religion, nationality or disabilities as protected by Italian Law (L.68/99).​ Reply is committed to ensuring that our candidate selection methods are fair and just. To help you during the recruitment process, please let us know of any Reasonable Adjustments you may need.*

# Manager, Statutory Reporting

Posted: October 26, 2026

Location
:   London

Job type
:   Full time

Requisition ID
:   REQ-9615

The Trade Desk is a global technology company and the world’s leading independent platform for digital advertising, with over 3,000 employees across more than 30 offices. Our technology helps advertisers reach the right audiences across the open internet — from streaming TV and podcasts to mobile apps, news, and more.   

Advertising powers the content people love. By making it more transparent, effective, and responsible, we help support trusted journalism, quality entertainment, and creators worldwide. The world’s brands and agencies rely on us to reach their customers and grow their businesses responsibly.   

The scale of our platform brings unique technical challenges — from processing massive datasets in real time to building systems that operate reliably on a global scale. When you work here, your impact is worldwide. We welcome diverse perspectives, encourage curiosity, and build teams that learn from one another. If you’re driven to solve meaningful challenges, we’d love to meet you.

**What you’ll do:**

Reporting to the Senior Manager, Statutory Reporting you will be responsible for supporting the Company’s annual EMEA compliance requirements while proactively ensuring accounting processes are compliant with global policies and procedures, within an effective internal control environment.

* Work directly with in-country service providers and internal teams with the review and filing of the following deliverables across the EMEA region:

+ Responsible for the compilation and review of the UK Annual statutory financial statements reporting under FRS101
+ Working with an external third party and internal FP&A teams to prepare business forecasts and undertake the annual impairment review of goodwill in accordance with IAS 36 - Impairment of Assets including audit readiness
+ Ownership of the US GAAP to Local GAAP bridge, ensuring all adjustments are clearly documented and supported
+ Manage the UK audit process during Planning, Interim, US Group (UK component) and Statutory phases of the audit acting as primary liaison with the external auditors and internal stakeholders
+ Manage the preparation and audit of annual statutory financial statements for all other EMEA entities where audits are required by maintaining strong working relationships with external auditors, management of internal teams ensuring deadlines are adhered to and fostering a strong control environment
+ Act as a trusted advisor to senior leadership, providing accounting guidance on business initiatives and strategic decisions
+ Ensure all financial statements are filed by required deadlines
+ Maintains up-to-date knowledge of accounting standards and monitors financial reporting changes across the EMEA region

* Management of a senior statutory accountant;
* Assist with maintaining the ERP statutory ledgers to ensure they adhere to filings and update with statutory adjustments as required;
* Work closely with the legal team to support company secretarial filings and compliance;
* Participation in other ad-hoc accounting projects as required;

**Who you are:**

* A qualified accountant (ACA/ACCA) from a top 20 practice background;
* 3+ years post qualified experience;
* People management skills and ability to coach and develop team members
* Strong knowledge of IFRS is required; Understanding of US GAAP is beneficial but not mandatory;
* Strong understanding of varied reporting environments across EMEA including documenting and explaining GAAP differences to senior stakeholders and US Group;
* Be able to demonstrate experience working in a multi-entity/multi-currency environment;
* Strong working knowledge of Microsoft Excel and AI tools;
